{"name":"Wooden Swing","hex":"#a58563","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wooden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of wood.","As if made of wood; moving awkwardly, or speaking with dull lack of emotion."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wooden"},{"term":"swing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To rotate about an off-centre fixed point.","To dance."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act, or an instance, of swinging.","The manner in which something is swung."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swing"}],"entries":[{"title":"Swing (seat)","blocks":[{"text":"A swing is a seat or platform, suspended from chains, ropes, or bars, on which one or more people can swing back and forth for enjoyment or relaxation. Swings are a common piece of equipment at children's playgrounds and may also be found in yards or gardens, on porches, inside homes, or as freestanding public play equipment like the Estonian village swing. Swings have a long history in many different parts of the world and come in various types."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/MoSchaukel.jpg/330px-MoSchaukel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swing_(seat)","wikidata":"Q188688"},{"title":"Wood","blocks":[{"text":"Wood is a structural tissue/material found as xylem in the stems and roots of trees and other woody plants. Being a natural material, it is characterized as an organic material – a natural composite of cellulosic fibers that are strong in tension and embedded in a matrix of lignin and hemicelluloses that resists compression."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/16_wood_samples.jpg/330px-16_wood_samples.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wood","wikidata":"Q287"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikim